# Control, not ownership. Bot2 casts Enduring Curiosity on turn 2 and Bot1 wins the flip of Invert Polarity (the first coin face is a win), so
# Bot1 controls it. On turn 3 Bot1's Misshapen Fiend hits Bot2 and Bot1 draws: "a creature you control" is read from the Curiosity's current
# controller. On turn 4 Bot2, the owner, Lightning Bolts it. It dies; its "when this dies" ability, controlled by Bot1, returns it "under its
# owner's control" (CR 400.3, 603.10a): the enchantment is Bot2's, not Bot1's. On turn 6 Bot2's Fiend hits Bot1 and now Bot2 draws, Bot1 not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Invert Polarity
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Misshapen Fiend
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Enduring Curiosity
Lightning Bolt
Misshapen Fiend
Island x13

